; PT10/ADR 0044, point 7: bounding box, generated geometry, transformations,
; snaps, distance and selection of a plain SOLID. Values by hand.
; Q: the figure v0, v1, v3, v2 is the rectangle (0,0) (4,0) (4,2) (0,2).
; T: three vertices, the fourth equal to the third.
Q = SOLID vertex=0,0 vertex=4,0 vertex=0,2 vertex=4,2
T = SOLID vertex=0,0 vertex=4,0 vertex=0,3 vertex=0,3
R = SOLID vertex=10,0 vertex=12,0 vertex=10,1 vertex=12,1 color=1
? bbox Q -> 0,0 4,2
? bbox T -> 0,0 4,3
; The generated geometry is the shape itself, with its effective properties.
? generated Q -> SOLID vertex=0,0 vertex=4,0 vertex=0,2 vertex=4,2
? generated T -> SOLID vertex=0,0 vertex=4,0 vertex=0,3 vertex=0,3
? generated R -> SOLID vertex=10,0 vertex=12,0 vertex=10,1 vertex=12,1 color=255,0,0
; The four vertices transformed, in the same order.
? transform Q move 1,1 -> SOLID vertex=1,1 vertex=5,1 vertex=1,3 vertex=5,3
; Rotation by 90 about the origin: (x,y) -> (-y,x).
? transform Q rotate 90 0,0 -> SOLID vertex=0,0 vertex=0,4 vertex=-2,0 vertex=-2,4
? transform Q scale 2 0,0 -> SOLID vertex=0,0 vertex=8,0 vertex=0,4 vertex=8,4
? transform Q scale 0 0,0 -> invalid
; A reflection does not change the order: v0, v1, v3, v2 is still the same region.
? transform Q mirror 0,0 0,1 -> SOLID vertex=0,0 vertex=-4,0 vertex=0,2 vertex=-4,2
? transform T mirror 0,5 1,5 -> SOLID vertex=0,10 vertex=4,10 vertex=0,7 vertex=0,7
; Endpoint snap on the distinct vertices only.
? snaps Q -> Endpoint 0,0; Endpoint 4,0; Endpoint 0,2; Endpoint 4,2
? snaps T -> Endpoint 0,0; Endpoint 4,0; Endpoint 0,3
; Distance 0 inside the figure and on its border, otherwise from the border.
? distance Q 2,1 -> 0
? distance Q 4,1 -> 0
? distance Q 6,1 -> 2
? distance Q 7,6 -> 5
? distance T 1,1 -> 0
; T is the triangle (0,0) (4,0) (0,3): its hypotenuse is 3x + 4y = 12.
? distance T 4,3 -> 2.4
; Window: the whole figure in the rectangle; crossing: the rectangle meets the
; figure, also when it lies inside it without touching the border.
? inside Q -1,-1 5,3 -> yes
? inside Q 1,-1 5,3 -> no
? crosses Q 1,0.5 2,1.5 -> yes
? crosses Q 5,0 6,2 -> no
? window -1,-1 5,4 -> Q T
? window -1,-1 13,4 -> Q T R
? crossing 1,0.5 2,1.5 -> Q T
? crossing 3,2.5 3.5,3 -> none
? crossing 10.5,0.2 11,0.8 -> R
; A click inside the figure picks it; outside, only within the tolerance.
? pick 11,0.5 tolerance=0.1 -> R
? pick 13,0.5 tolerance=0.5 -> none
? pick 13,0.5 tolerance=1.5 -> R
? snap 3.9,1.9 aperture=0.5 -> Endpoint 4,2
